<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Trip</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Thief (guild level 7)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>trip &lt;someone&gt;
trip            (whoever you are fighting)
</pre>
<p>Hooks your opponent's legs out from under them, so they lose their next 
round of the fight: a moment to strike, or to get away. It costs 10 
endurance, and it is an attack: they will fight you for it.
</p><p>Your dexterity and skill against theirs decide it. Fumble, and you 
stumble yourself, losing half a round or a whole one. Someone you have 
just tripped watches for it, and leaps over your leg if you try again 
too soon.
</p><p>Only people and other mammals can be tripped; you can't trip a snake, a 
spider or a ghost. Nor can you trip someone far heavier than you, or 
someone already lying down. To trip another player, both of you must have 
signed the Book of Blood.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
